# Click, double-click (word), triple-click (paragraph), drag, shift-click.
open "$DIR/chapter.md"
click_index 4
expect selection 4 4
wait 30
click_index 5 2
expect selection 4 7
wait 30
click_index 150 3
expect selection 0 235
wait 30
drag_index 147 157
expect selection 147 157
type "beacon"
expect text "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Zoë Ångström stood at the top of the beacon stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
wait 30
click_index 110
wait 30
click_index 113 shift
expect selection 110 113
type "Ada"
expect text "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Ada Ångström stood at the top of the beacon stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
shot mouse
# Clicking far below the text puts the caret at the end.
wait 30
click 600 780
expect cursor 260
# Clicking in the Explorer takes focus from the editor: typing is ignored.
wait 30
click 100 400
type "ignored"
expect text "The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Ada Ångström stood at the top of the beacon stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
# Clicking back into the editor restores focus; queued keys were discarded.
wait 30
click_index 0
type "~"
expect text "~The fog came in off the fjord the way it always did in late October: quietly, completely, and without asking. Ada Ångström stood at the top of the beacon stairs with a lantern in one hand and her grandmother’s letter in the other.\n\n“You’re late,” said Dvořák.\n"
